{{Short description|Final stage of the competition}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=May 2018}}
The knockout stage of the [[1954 FIFA World Cup]] was the second and final stage of the competition, following the group stage. The knockout stage began on 26 June with the quarter-finals and ended on 4 July 1954 with the [[1954 FIFA World Cup final|final match]], held at the [[Wankdorf Stadium]] in [[Bern]]. The top two teams from each group (eight in total) advanced to the knockout stage to compete in a [[Single-elimination tournament|single-elimination]] style tournament. A match for third place also was played between the two losing teams of the semi-finals.

[[Germany national football team|West Germany]] won the final 3–2 against [[Hungary national football team|Hungary]] for their first World Cup title.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.thehardtackle.com/2012/a-game-that-changed-germany-and-hungary-forever-the-miracle-of-bern//|title=The miracle of Bern – a game that changed Germany and Hungary forever|first=Amlan|last=Majundar|publisher=theHardTackle|date=11 October 2012|access-date=7 December 2016}}</ref>

